  "query_preview": "Forecast Discussion...\n\nGoing into the extended portion of the forecast period, the \nteleconnection pattern is forecast to be in a -AO/-NAO/+PNA/neutral \nEPO configuration.  Fairly progressive upper level pattern aloft \nwill likely keep a steady flow of perturbations moving across the \ncountry.  Updated signal analysis shows a signal passage around \nThanksgiving, which will likely produce some sort of SE US storm \nsystem.  Combination of physics based and AI guidance suggests a \nfairly cloudy period for the Thanksgiving holidays with a chance of \nshowers with the passing signal.  Not much cold air available and \nrecent AI guidance suggests fairly seasonal temps for highs, though \novernight lows probably will run above normal given anticipated \ncloud cover.  Another signal passage looks to occur toward the end \nof the month and may deliver some colder weather going into December \nas the -AO/-NAO/+PNA pattern looks to continue.  The EPO remains \nuncertain as current model trends keep it rather positive which \nwould lead me to believe that any colder air will be transient in \nnature.  Model predictability here still only has about a 6-8 day \nlead time.",
